{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 43, :comments ["<b>And HaShem said, etc. This is the statute of the Pesach.</b> It is difficult: why did He not say ״דַּבֵּר אֶל בְּנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל״ as is the pattern stated for every single commandment? According to what we have written (Exodus 12:3), that this passage was spoken on the fourteenth of Nisan, there was no need to say ״דַּבֵּר״ since it is adjacent to ״דַּבְּרוּ אֶל כָּל עֲדַת יִשְׂרָאֵל״ that He said there. And one may give a reason why it was not written in its [chronological] place: since this commandment in its completeness is [also] like the Pesach of generations, it was stated after the Exodus from Egypt, to say that all of this in its entirety is a prerequisite for all generations." "<b>And I saw</b> a midrash of our Rabbis (Exodus Rabbah 19:5) that HaShem brought forth a spirit from the Garden of Eden, and perfumed Moses' Pesach, and all Israel gathered and said to him: Moses our master, please, feed us from your Pesach. He said to them: if you are not circumcised you may not eat, as it is written ״זֹאת חֻקַּת הַפָּסַח״ etc. Immediately they submitted themselves and were circumcised, etc. — thus far. Now according to this midrash it is not difficult why He did not say ״דַּבֵּר״ etc. or ״לֵאמֹר״, because this passage was spoken to Moses and to Aaron, and He commanded them ״כָּל בֶּן נֵכָר״ etc., and after Israel came to partake of Moses' perfumed Pesach they circumcised themselves." "<b>And it is difficult</b> according to the words of the midrash: how could he give them of his Pesach, when the Pesach may be eaten only by those registered for it? Perhaps he said this to them only so that they would circumcise themselves, and once they circumcised themselves their own paschal offerings would likewise be perfumed like Moses' Pesach. And I saw proof for the words of the midrash that they did not wish to circumcise, from what is said in Ezekiel (20:8): ״וַיַּמְרוּ בִי וְלֹא אָבוּ לִשְׁמֹעַ אֵלַי״ etc. ״וָאוֹמַר לִשְׁפֹּךְ חֲמָתִי עֲלֵיהֶם בְּתוֹךְ אֶרֶץ מִצְרָיִם״ — behold, they did not accept to perform His commandments, may He be blessed."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:27:26.924819237Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}